A||N||14||FieroKyle||Fiero Store's Sprint Manifold questions.||||1||
Z||000000||FieroKyle||11-05-2001||01:10 AM||||Alright, as this is my first year with a Fiero and therefore storing it all winter, I am gonna be saving a lot of money in insurance and the usual for it at the parts store every weekend. I have a bad exhaust leak and now probably need a new exhaust. I figure also if I am gonna be doing that, why not upgrade the manifold to the sprints. I am asking if they make much difference at all in overall performance and sound. You guys feel an actual difference any whats like some dyno numbers if anyone has them with them like a before and after. Also #2 is they are asking I think $500 for them, is there anywhere else to get the same ones but possible cheapper? Feel free to private message me or reply to the post. Thanks!<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0PgAgVMwT!1W9RUb20vChbvv6QaE!2K1LWrFB6SxTnTchZgvIygv7Y3YwXpVdD8GeNkWpurYfoQxvNRK6j6kEmOFLoIHavbIr/Kyle-85-GT.jpg">    <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||11-05-2001||02:48 AM||||I have the Sprints. As for real gains (Dyno) I haven't had my car tested. I do know that the car runs a lot better and sounds a little deeper tone. Chris West also has "Shorty" headers. His are a little less expensive, but they are not jet coated. To add coating, they cost about the same. The Fiero Store will take off 10% if you belong to a Fiero Club. (They consider Pennock's a club  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  )<BR>I originally bought mine when they first came out in 1994/1995. Aside from being less restrictive they won't crack like stock ones and they look better. There is some discussion as to how much gain they really produce and speculation that porting the stock ones has the same gain. But to me the Sprints are better than the ported stock ones due to the tuned individual runners. Any headers you buy for a Fiero are expensive. Full headers are good if you plan on doing work to the engine,using a turbo, Supercharger, NO2 spray or going to a 3.4L, But on a stock 2.8L you will gain horsepower but lose torque. I think 1FST2M6 has some dyno figures for the full headers and ported stock. Not sure if he ever tested Sprints.<P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">          <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||11-05-2001||06:58 AM||||To have your old manifolds welded(if even cracked) is about $30 and a couple of grinding stones is an additional $15 - time free.<BR>Sprints $500.<BR>Performance about the same.||||reg||1
Z||000003||RiceCooker||11-05-2001||04:33 PM||||Most people do not think they're worth the price - especially if you have to convert from Canadian $$$. If you are tight on money, it might be better spent but i love mine. They look cool but i wouldn't say i got any huge gains. <BR>Oreif is correct on the specifics.<BR>I can't say how much they changed the sound becasue at the same time, i put in 2 1/4" exhaust minus the cat and plus flowmaster muffler and i cant tell you how awesome it sounds. If i can't afford the V8, i might as well have the V8 sound, eh?<BR>They're more or less another toy for my car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Voytek||11-05-2001||05:29 PM||||I've got a set too.  I haven't noticed any significant power increase.  My old manifolds were not ported, so going with Sprints made a bit of a difference.  Sound?  Changing the headers alone, actually made my car sound smoother if a bit deeper but definitely not more aggressive.  Looks?  Can't beat that.  They make the engine look like a muscle car.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Keep in mind, perhaps they make more of a difference if you also install a performance exhaust system.  I know RiceCooker's complete system definitely made a difference.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroKyle||11-05-2001||10:47 PM||||So as far as power increase, you guys are neh to it, but for looks, sound, and may be a bit of difference in perf. its worth it? Well I am just want to keep the engine getting better. Would love to have a Archie Special in there, but I don't see that happening in the near future. Until then I am just gonna dress the car up and keep it mint like it is. Now I have a second car, its gonna be my weekend cruiser. Anything that goes bad on it, I want replace it with the same part except better. Anyways I want add over over this next year, new quarter windows, the manifolds, new exhaust, the big bore intake. Future projects might include putting a turbo, or boring it out, or NOS. Money and the future will only decide.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Dave Gunsul||11-06-2001||12:40 AM||||Hey Kyle, Darrell Morse ports the exhaust manifolds for $150.00 and that includes return shipping. <BR>Darrells email: morse86@aol.com<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
